    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2761" root="بطر" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِيَطْرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْطَارٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <i>A tailor.</i> (Sh,
S, * K.) A poet says, (calling a tailor a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بيطر</span>, like
as one calls a skilful man an <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِسْكَاف</span>, Sh, TA,)
“<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَقَّ البِيَطْرِ مِدْرَعَ الهُمَامِ</span><br />
”
[<i>Like as the tailor cuts lengthwise,</i> or <i>slits, the
woollen tunic of the valiant chief</i>]. (Sh, S.)

